# function Meter() {}  class Fine extends Meter { read() { return super.read(); } }
# A lookup through super starts at the prototype object of Meter. The guards of a constructor function begin with the first object that it makes and speak of the prototype object that it has then,
# so the lookup also asks for the guard of the function's prototype property: that one is waited for, and it ends when the function gets another prototype object.
# Nothing is asked where the function keeps its prototype object and the member is proven
